      "title": "Signal-PDU, Some/IP: Deregister fields and their arrays later",
      "message": "Signal-PDU, Some/IP: Deregister fields and their arrays later\n\nDon't call proto_free_deregistered_fields() from a dissector,\nincluding in prefs, because there can be a tree which refers\nto its dynamically registered fields (perhaps interesting fields\nto a Lua field extractor.) Wireshark will free those fields at\nan appropriate safe time, such as when redissecting.\n\nWe still need to set the dynamic hf arrays to NULL so that the\ndissector doesn't refer to them, but don't want to leak them. That\nis what proto_add_deregistered_data is for - it will free those\narrays at the time that the fields are actually freed.\n\nFix #20425\n",
      "author_name": "John Thacker",
      "author_email": "johnthacker@gmail.com",
      "authored_date": "2025-03-08T07:38:00.000-05:00",
      "committer_name": "John Thacker",
      "committer_email": "johnthacker@gmail.com",
